    <heading level="1">Everyday Math</heading>
    <exercise number="215" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Mental math You can use binomial multiplication to multiply numbers without a calculator. Say you need to multiply $$13$$ times $$15.$$ Think of $$13$$ as $$10 + 3$$ and $$15$$ as $$10 + 5.$$</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ Multiply $$(10 + 3)(10 + 5)$$ by the FOIL method.</item>
          <item>ⓑ Multiply $$13 \cdot 15$$ without using a calculator.</item>
          <item>ⓒ Which way is easier for you? Why?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ 195</item>
          <item>ⓑ 195</item>
          <item>ⓒ Answers will vary.</item>
        </list>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="216" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Mental math You can use binomial multiplication to multiply numbers without a calculator. Say you need to multiply $$18$$ times $$17.$$ Think of $$18$$ as $$20 - 2$$ and $$17$$ as $$20 - 3.$$</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ Multiply $$(20 - 2)(20 - 3)$$ by the FOIL method.</item>
          <item>ⓑ Multiply $$18 \cdot 17$$ without using a calculator.</item>
          <item>ⓒ Which way is easier for you? Why?</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
